before:
```html
<section class="shelf"><p id="near">Near note</p><div><p id="deep">Nested note</p></div></section><p id="after">After shelf</p><p id="later">Later note</p>
```

```css
p { color: navy; }
.shelf > p { color: teal; }
.shelf + p { color: purple; }
```

after:
The `>` sign chooses only direct children.

```css
.shelf > p {
  color: teal;
}
```

This makes a paragraph teal when its parent has the `shelf` class. A paragraph inside a `div` inside the shelf does not match. Its parent is the `div`.

Siblings are parts with the same parent. The `+` sign chooses the next sibling only. The `~` sign can choose any matching sibling that comes later.

```css
.shelf ~ p {
  color: purple;
}
```

This chooses paragraphs after the shelf that share its parent. It does not choose paragraphs inside the shelf or before it.
